    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a human-readable `telephoneDisplay` field to the Owner API response while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**What I found:** This is Spring PetClinic REST. Owner DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml`, and `OwnerMapper` (MapStruct) auto-maps derived getters by name (like `contactPreference`, `ageBand`) \u2014 so a new getter plus a matching schema field is all that's needed. The `Owner` model already had `countryCodeOf()`/`nationalNumberLength()` helpers for the E.164 country code.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` that splits the stored E.164 number into its country code and national digits, then emits the country code, a space, and the national digits grouped in threes (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). It falls back to the raw value if the number is null or has no recognised country code.\n\nMapStruct picks the new getter up automatically (no explicit `@Mapping` needed). The acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes: `telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`.",
